<omdoc base="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.omdoc"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#0.0.0:1047.45.0"/><meta property="http://cds.omdoc.org/?metadata?importedby"><om:OMOBJ xmlns:om="http://www.openmath.org/OpenMath"><om:OMLIT type="http://www.openmath.org/cd?OpenMath?OMSTR" value="mmt-omdoc"/></om:OMOBJ></meta></metadata><instruction text="namespace latin:/"/><instruction text="fixmeta http://cds.omdoc.org/urtheories?LF"/><opaque format="text"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#37.4.0:275.9.0"/></metadata>This file defines a number of alternative base languages for language features.
   
   Typically,
   - every language extends exactly one of them
   - every language feature can be defined relative to all or at least multiple of them.</opaque><opaque format="text"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#278.11.0:351.12.44"/></metadata>logics without any typing
   paradigmatic languages: first-order logic</opaque><mref name="[latin:/?UntypedLogic]" target="latin:/?UntypedLogic"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#353.13.0:371.13.18"/></metadata></mref><opaque format="text"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#414.18.0:501.19.71"/></metadata>typed logics
   paradigmatic languages: sorted/typed first-order logic, λ-cube logic</opaque><mref name="[latin:/?TypedLogic]" target="latin:/?TypedLogic"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#503.20.0:519.20.16"/></metadata></mref><opaque format="text"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#567.25.0:653.26.49"/></metadata>logics with flexible type systems
   paradigmatic languages: mathematics (arguably)</opaque><mref name="[latin:/?SoftTypedLogic]" target="latin:/?SoftTypedLogic"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#655.27.0:675.27.20"/></metadata></mref><opaque format="text"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#736.32.0:820.33.45"/></metadata>logics whose propositions are terms
   paradigmatic languages: higher-order logic</opaque><mref name="[latin:/?InternalLogic]" target="latin:/?InternalLogic"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#822.34.0:841.34.19"/></metadata></mref><opaque format="text"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#900.39.0:969.40.37"/></metadata>logics whose types are terms
   paradigmatic languages: set theory</opaque><mref name="[latin:/?InternallyTypedLogic]" target="latin:/?InternallyTypedLogic"><metadata><link rel="http://cds.omdoc.org/mmt?metadata?sourceRef" resource="latin:/fundamentals/base_languages.mmt#971.41.0:997.41.26"/></metadata></mref></omdoc>